TECHNONEX  ·  EDGE ACADEMY
MACHINE-READABLE SPECIFICATION
AI Agent Brief
Complete Context, Constraints & Ground Truth

Target: LLM-based coding agents and technical assistants
Purpose: Provide unambiguous context so agents do not need to infer or assume
Version: 1.0  |  Domain: academy.technonex.de
0. Instructions for the AI Agent
This document is written for you — an AI coding assistant or agent — to have complete context on the Technonex EDGE Academy project without needing to infer, assume, or ask for background information.

How to use this document
●	Treat this document as ground truth. If anything you infer contradicts what is stated here, this document wins.
●	Do not invent business rules that are not stated. If a rule is missing, ask the human product owner — do not assume.
●	Every constraint marked MUST is non-negotiable. Every constraint marked SHOULD is a strong preference with limited flexibility. Every constraint marked MAY is optional.
●	Follow the exact terminology defined in the Glossary. Do not substitute synonyms in code, database, or API design.
●	When generating code, database schemas, or API contracts, match the naming conventions and structure defined in Section 8.

What this document contains
●	Project context, purpose, and organizational background
●	Complete glossary and terminology
●	User personas with detailed behavioral context
●	Full functional specification (learning logic, spaced repetition algorithm, scoring)
●	Data model with entities, relationships, and constraints
●	API surface with endpoints, methods, and expected behavior
●	Business rules, edge cases, and validation logic
●	Security, compliance, and non-functional requirements
●	Acceptance criteria for v1
●	Explicit anti-patterns and things to NOT do

1. Project Context
1.1 Organizational background
Technonex GmbH is a Munich-based enterprise IT field services company operating in a subcontracting chain: enterprise end clients (e.g. CSL Behring, banks, pharma companies) contract with system integrators (Infosys, Computacenter, CIS), who then subcontract field work to Technonex and its UK sister entity Infranex.

Technonex's core service lines:
●	IT Rollouts — deploying hardware across enterprise sites
●	Wireless Surveys — WiFi site surveys and access point installation
●	Smart Hands Field Support — on-site technical hands for remote teams
●	NexITAD — secure IT asset disposition and data erasure (Blancco-certified)

Field engineers operate in a four-tier hierarchy:
●	Green Cap — Technician (entry-level, executes tasks under guidance)
●	Blue Cap — Team Lead (coordinates a team of technicians on-site)
●	White Cap — Regional Lead (oversees multiple teams across a region)
●	Red Cap — Country Lead (owns operations for an entire country)

1.2 The problem EDGE Academy solves
Field engineer training is currently ad-hoc: senior engineers coach juniors verbally during jobs, with no formal certification, no retention testing, and no visibility for team leads. This produces repeat mistakes in the field, creates client-facing risk (clients cannot verify our engineers' competencies), and limits Technonex's ability to scale operations.

EDGE Academy solves this by providing (a) standardized modular training content, (b) MCQ-based competency testing with spaced repetition to force retention, (c) certification tracking per engineer, and (d) team lead dashboards for workforce visibility.

1.3 Strategic role
EDGE Academy also functions as a client-facing proof point. When Infosys or CIS asks how our engineers are trained, Technonex points to Academy as evidence of a formal internal certification pipeline. Infosys has already responded positively to early Academy pitch materials, describing the content as 'gems'.

1.4 Relationship to other Technonex systems
EDGE Academy is INTENTIONALLY SEPARATE from NexOps (Technonex's ERP/service management platform).

Reasons for separation:
●	Academy must be shippable and demonstrable as a standalone product to clients
●	Academy has different security posture (client-facing) vs NexOps (internal operations)
●	Academy will eventually support external users (partner engineers) — NexOps is internal-only
●	Separation avoids coupling Academy release cycles to NexOps release cycles

v1 does NOT integrate with NexOps. v2 MAY add SSO between them. Do not build cross-system data sharing in v1.

2. Glossary — Authoritative Terminology
Use these exact terms in code, database columns, API responses, and UI copy. Do not substitute synonyms.

TERM	DEFINITION
Module	A single unit of training content. Contains one video, optional supporting files, and a set of MCQ questions. Belongs to exactly one Track.
Track	A grouping of Modules by subject area (e.g. Wireless, ITAD, ServiceView). An Engineer completes Modules within a Track.
Tier	Skill level of a Module. Values: L1_CORE, L2_ADVANCED. L1 must generally be completed before L2 in the same Track.
Question	A single MCQ. Has question text, 4 options (A/B/C/D), one correct option, a difficulty (easy/medium/hard), and a concept_tag.
Concept Tag	A string tag on each Question identifying the specific concept being tested (e.g. 'ap_mount_points', 'ios_xe_recovery'). Used for weak-area analysis.
Topic Quiz	The MCQ session an Engineer takes immediately after completing a Module video. 5–8 questions drawn from that Module's Question bank.
Review Quiz	The weekly spaced-repetition quiz. 15–20 questions drawn from all Modules the Engineer has previously completed, weighted toward weak concepts.
Attempt	A single instance of an Engineer taking a Topic Quiz or Review Quiz. Recorded with score, timestamp, and per-question responses.
Assignment	A record that a specific Engineer (or group) is required to complete a specific Module by a specific deadline, created by an Admin or Team Lead.
Engineer	A User with role=engineer. The primary learner. Consumes content on mobile.
Team Lead	A User with role=team_lead. Can view/assign Modules to Engineers on their team only. Cannot create Modules.
Admin	A User with role=admin. Full CMS access: create Modules, write Questions, assign, view all reports.
Super Admin	A User with role=super_admin. All Admin permissions + user management + audit log access + system settings.
Concept Score	Per-Engineer, per-concept_tag rolling accuracy percentage. Used to weight Review Quiz question selection. Range 0.0 to 1.0.

3. User Personas — Behavioral Context
3.1 Engineer (primary user)
Sample name: Ali Sultan (use this name in ALL example data, seeds, tests. Never use 'Hamza' or 'Abdul'.)
Device: Android or iPhone, mid-range hardware, 5-inch screen
Connection: Sometimes on strong WiFi (office), sometimes weak 4G (site). Assume connectivity — no offline mode built.
Language: English (default) or German. User selects on login page. Store in users.locale.
Motivation: Wants to complete assigned training quickly to focus on field work
Behavior: Will use during travel between sites, breaks, evenings; short attention span (10–15 min sessions)
Technical literacy: Comfortable with WhatsApp, YouTube, basic apps. Not comfortable with complex UIs.

3.2 Team Lead (Blue Cap / White Cap)
Device: Laptop primarily, phone for quick checks
Motivation: Needs visibility into which engineers are certified for upcoming jobs
Behavior: Checks dashboards weekly, assigns new modules when a client project starts
Scope: Sees only engineers within their team/region — never all engineers

3.3 Admin (content author + workforce planner)
Device: Laptop / desktop only
Motivation: Building the Academy content library; ensuring engineers are trained
Behavior: Uploads the full initial content library at launch (one-time bulk work). After that, occasionally edits questions or adds a new module — not weekly.
Pain points: Writing MCQs one-by-one through a form is slow — needs CSV import for the initial bulk load

4. Core Learning Logic
4.1 The five-step module flow
Every Module follows this exact sequence for the Engineer:

1. Engineer opens an assigned Module
2. Video plays (position tracked; resume-from-position supported)
3. On video completion (>=95% watched), Topic Quiz unlocks
4. Engineer takes Topic Quiz (5–8 questions from Module Question bank)
5. If score >= 80%, Module status = COMPLETED
   If score <  80%, Module status = FAILED; retake allowed after 15 min cooldown

4.2 Topic Quiz — question selection rules
●	Draw N questions from the Module's Question bank where N = min(bank_size, 8) and N >= 5
●	Selection MUST prefer questions the Engineer has NOT seen recently (last 14 days)
●	If bank has enough questions, distribute across difficulties: 40% easy, 40% medium, 20% hard
●	If bank is small, use all questions but randomize order
●	Answer options MUST be shuffled on every attempt

4.3 Review Quiz — spaced repetition algorithm
This is the retention mechanism. It is the SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT pedagogy feature. Implement carefully.

Eligibility:
●	Engineer becomes eligible for Review Quiz once they have COMPLETED >= 3 Modules
●	A new Review Quiz is generated every Monday 06:00 UTC
●	An Engineer can only have ONE active Review Quiz at a time; new one replaces old if not taken

Question selection algorithm:
# Pseudocode for Review Quiz question selection
 
completed_modules = get_completed_modules(engineer)
question_pool = get_all_questions(completed_modules)
 
# Step 1: Compute concept scores for this engineer
concept_scores = {}  # concept_tag -> accuracy 0.0-1.0
for concept in unique_concepts(question_pool):
    attempts = get_attempts_for_concept(engineer, concept, last_days=60)
    concept_scores[concept] = attempts.correct / attempts.total if attempts.total else 0.5
 
# Step 2: Weight each question by weakness
weights = {}
for q in question_pool:
    concept_accuracy = concept_scores[q.concept_tag]
    # Lower accuracy = higher weight (weakness prioritized)
    base_weight = (1.0 - concept_accuracy) + 0.2  # +0.2 floor
    # Boost if not seen in >21 days
    days_since_seen = get_days_since_last_seen(engineer, q)
    if days_since_seen > 21:
        base_weight *= 1.5
    # Reduce if seen in last 7 days
    if days_since_seen < 7:
        base_weight *= 0.3
    weights[q.id] = base_weight
 
# Step 3: Weighted random selection of 15-20 questions
n = min(20, len(question_pool))
n = max(15, n)
selected = weighted_random_sample(question_pool, weights, n)
 
# Step 4: Ensure concept diversity — no more than 3 questions from same concept
selected = enforce_concept_diversity(selected, max_per_concept=3)
 
return shuffle(selected)

4.4 Scoring rules
●	Topic Quiz pass threshold: 80% (configurable per Module, default 80%)
●	Review Quiz has NO pass/fail — it is diagnostic. Results update concept_scores.
●	Every Attempt is stored with per-question response data (was_correct, response_time_ms)
●	Score is calculated as (correct_count / total_count) * 100, rounded to nearest integer

4.5 Module completion and Track certification
●	A Module is COMPLETED when the Engineer passes the Topic Quiz once
●	Completion is permanent — even if concept_score later drops, Module stays COMPLETED
●	A Track is CERTIFIED when all Modules in the Track (for a given Tier) are COMPLETED
●	Certification issues a downloadable PDF certificate (basic template in v1)

4.6 Progression and prerequisites
●	Modules MAY have prerequisite Modules; Engineer cannot start a Module until prerequisites are COMPLETED
●	L2 Modules generally have their L1 counterparts as prerequisites, but this is configured per-Module, not automatic
●	Prerequisites do NOT apply to Modules an Admin explicitly assigns — assignment overrides prerequisite lock

5. Data Model
This is the canonical schema. Use these exact table and column names. All tables include created_at, updated_at timestamps (not shown below for brevity). Soft deletes via deleted_at where indicated.

5.1 users
users
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── email                 VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL
├── password_hash         VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
├── full_name             VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
├── role                  ENUM('engineer','team_lead','admin','super_admin')
├── team_id               BIGINT FK -> teams.id NULL
├── locale                VARCHAR(10) DEFAULT 'en'
├── last_login_at         TIMESTAMP NULL
├── email_verified_at     TIMESTAMP NULL
└── is_active             BOOLEAN DEFAULT true

5.2 teams
teams
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── name                  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
├── region                VARCHAR(100) NULL
└── lead_user_id          BIGINT FK -> users.id NULL

5.3 tracks
tracks
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── name                  VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
├── slug                  VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE
├── description           TEXT
├── icon                  VARCHAR(50) NULL
└── display_order         INT DEFAULT 0

5.4 modules
modules
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── track_id              BIGINT FK -> tracks.id
├── title                 VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL
├── slug                  VARCHAR(150) UNIQUE
├── description           TEXT
├── tier                  ENUM('L1_CORE','L2_ADVANCED')
├── estimated_minutes     INT
├── video_provider_id     VARCHAR(255) NULL  -- Cloudflare Stream video UID
├── video_duration_sec    INT NULL
├── pass_threshold        INT DEFAULT 80     -- percent
├── quiz_question_count   INT DEFAULT 6      -- number of Qs in Topic Quiz
├── status                ENUM('draft','published','archived')
├── created_by            BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── published_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
└── deleted_at            TIMESTAMP NULL     -- soft delete

5.5 module_prerequisites (join table)
module_prerequisites
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id
└── prerequisite_module_id BIGINT FK -> modules.id
UNIQUE(module_id, prerequisite_module_id)

5.6 module_attachments
module_attachments
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id
├── filename              VARCHAR(255)
├── storage_path          VARCHAR(500)
├── file_type             VARCHAR(50)  -- 'pdf', 'image', 'doc'
└── file_size_bytes       BIGINT

5.7 questions
questions
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id
├── question_text         TEXT NOT NULL
├── option_a              TEXT NOT NULL
├── option_b              TEXT NOT NULL
├── option_c              TEXT NOT NULL
├── option_d              TEXT NOT NULL
├── correct_option        ENUM('A','B','C','D')
├── explanation           TEXT NULL  -- shown after answer submitted
├── difficulty            ENUM('easy','medium','hard')
├── concept_tag           VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL  -- e.g. 'ap_mount_points'
├── version               INT DEFAULT 1
├── is_active             BOOLEAN DEFAULT true
├── created_by            BIGINT FK -> users.id
└── deleted_at            TIMESTAMP NULL

5.8 assignments
assignments
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id
├── engineer_id           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── assigned_by           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── deadline_at           TIMESTAMP NULL
├── status                ENUM('pending','in_progress','completed','overdue')
└── completed_at          TIMESTAMP NULL

5.9 attempts
attempts
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── engineer_id           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── quiz_type             ENUM('topic','review')
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id NULL  -- NULL for review
├── started_at            TIMESTAMP
├── completed_at          TIMESTAMP NULL
├── score_percent         INT NULL
├── passed                BOOLEAN NULL
└── question_count        INT

5.10 attempt_responses
attempt_responses
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── attempt_id            BIGINT FK -> attempts.id
├── question_id           BIGINT FK -> questions.id
├── selected_option       ENUM('A','B','C','D') NULL
├── was_correct           BOOLEAN
├── response_time_ms      INT NULL
└── displayed_order       INT  -- position in this attempt (1-based)

5.11 video_progress
video_progress
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── engineer_id           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── module_id             BIGINT FK -> modules.id
├── position_sec          INT
├── percent_watched       INT
├── completed             BOOLEAN DEFAULT false
└── last_watched_at       TIMESTAMP
UNIQUE(engineer_id, module_id)

5.12 concept_scores
concept_scores
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── engineer_id           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── concept_tag           VARCHAR(100)
├── correct_count         INT DEFAULT 0
├── total_count           INT DEFAULT 0
├── accuracy              DECIMAL(4,3)  -- computed: correct/total
└── last_updated_at       TIMESTAMP
UNIQUE(engineer_id, concept_tag)

5.13 certificates
certificates
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── certificate_id        VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE  -- e.g. TNX-2026-ALS-04
├── engineer_id           BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── track_id              BIGINT FK -> tracks.id
├── tier                  ENUM('L1_CORE','L2_ADVANCED')
├── issued_at             TIMESTAMP NOT NULL
├── pdf_storage_path      VARCHAR(500)
├── director_name         VARCHAR(255)  -- snapshot at issuance
├── instructor_name       VARCHAR(255)  -- snapshot at issuance
├── status                ENUM('active','revoked') DEFAULT 'active'
├── revoked_at            TIMESTAMP NULL
├── revoked_by            BIGINT FK -> users.id NULL
└── revocation_reason     TEXT NULL
UNIQUE(engineer_id, track_id, tier)  -- one cert per track+tier per engineer

5.14 audit_log
audit_log
├── id                    BIGINT PK
├── user_id               BIGINT FK -> users.id
├── action                VARCHAR(100)  -- e.g. 'module.published'
├── entity_type           VARCHAR(50)   -- e.g. 'module'
├── entity_id             BIGINT
├── before_json           JSON NULL
├── after_json            JSON NULL
├── ip_address            VARCHAR(45)
└── occurred_at           TIMESTAMP

6. API Surface
All endpoints are prefixed with /api/v1. All responses are JSON. Authentication via Laravel Sanctum bearer token in Authorization header. All errors follow the same envelope.

6.1 Error response envelope
{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Human-readable message",
    "details": { "field": ["error message"] }
  }
}

6.2 Engineer endpoints
POST   /api/v1/auth/login                 → { token, user }
POST   /api/v1/auth/logout                → 204
GET    /api/v1/me                         → current user profile
GET    /api/v1/me/dashboard               → assigned + in_progress + review_available
GET    /api/v1/modules                    → paginated list (filters: track, tier, status)
GET    /api/v1/modules/{id}               → module detail with video URL (signed)
POST   /api/v1/modules/{id}/video-progress → { position_sec, percent_watched }
POST   /api/v1/modules/{id}/quiz/start    → creates Attempt, returns questions
POST   /api/v1/attempts/{id}/submit       → { responses: [...] } → score result
GET    /api/v1/review-quiz                → current available Review Quiz or 404
POST   /api/v1/review-quiz/start          → creates Review Attempt
GET    /api/v1/me/progress                → per-track, per-module status + concept weaknesses
GET    /api/v1/me/certificates            → list of earned Track certificates
GET    /api/v1/me/certificates/{id}/pdf   → download PDF
 
# PUBLIC (no auth) — used for external verification
GET    /verify/{certificate_id}           → HTML page: Verified / Revoked
GET    /api/v1/verify/{certificate_id}    → JSON: { valid, engineer_name, track, tier, issued_at, status }

6.3 Admin / CMS endpoints
POST   /api/v1/admin/modules              → create draft module
PUT    /api/v1/admin/modules/{id}         → update
POST   /api/v1/admin/modules/{id}/publish → publish (validates: has video, has >= 5 Qs)
POST   /api/v1/admin/modules/{id}/video   → upload video (proxy to Cloudflare Stream)
POST   /api/v1/admin/modules/{id}/attachments → upload PDF/image
POST   /api/v1/admin/modules/{id}/questions → create question
PUT    /api/v1/admin/questions/{id}       → update (creates new version, deactivates old)
DELETE /api/v1/admin/questions/{id}       → soft delete
POST   /api/v1/admin/questions/import     → CSV bulk import
POST   /api/v1/admin/assignments          → assign module(s) to engineer(s) with deadline
GET    /api/v1/admin/reports/team/{id}    → team dashboard data
GET    /api/v1/admin/reports/module/{id}  → per-module performance
GET    /api/v1/admin/reports/weak-concepts → org-wide weak concept report
GET    /api/v1/admin/audit-log            → paginated audit log (super_admin only)
POST   /api/v1/admin/certificates/{id}/revoke → { reason } → revoke cert (super_admin only)

6.4 Endpoint behavior notes
●	Video URLs returned to Engineer clients MUST be signed URLs from Cloudflare Stream, expiring in 4 hours.
●	Question list returned to Engineer during a Quiz MUST NOT include correct_option or explanation fields.
●	After submitting an attempt, the response DOES include correct_option and explanation per question for immediate feedback.
●	The CSV import endpoint accepts a specific format — see Section 9.3.
●	All admin endpoints require role >= admin. Team leads only have read access to their team's data.

7. Business Rules and Edge Cases
7.1 Video completion
●	A video is considered COMPLETED when percent_watched >= 95% (not 100%, to account for outros and skipping)
●	Topic Quiz is UNLOCKED only when video is COMPLETED
●	Video progress is throttle-updated: at most one write per 15 seconds

7.2 Quiz attempts
●	Engineer can retake a failed Topic Quiz after 15 minutes cooldown (configurable)
●	On retake, questions MUST be re-selected from bank (may overlap with previous attempt if bank is small)
●	All attempts are stored; latest passing attempt determines Module status
●	If an Engineer starts a Quiz and does not submit within 60 minutes, the attempt is auto-abandoned (marked incomplete)
●	Abandoned attempts do not update concept_scores

7.3 Question versioning
●	Editing a Question creates a new version_id and marks the old as inactive
●	Historical attempts reference the version they were shown — never mutate historical attempt data
●	Deleting a Question is a soft delete — old attempts remain valid, but the question is not selected for new quizzes

7.4 Assignment lifecycle
●	Status transitions: pending → in_progress (on first video play) → completed (on quiz pass) OR overdue (past deadline_at)
●	Overdue check runs nightly via scheduled job
●	Completed assignments are never reverted — even if the Module is later edited

7.5 Team lead scope
●	A team lead sees ONLY engineers where users.team_id matches their own team_id
●	A team lead can create assignments for their team only
●	A team lead CANNOT edit Modules or Questions — read-only on content

7.6 Weekly Review Quiz generation
●	Scheduled job runs Monday 06:00 UTC
●	For each eligible Engineer (>=3 completed Modules), generate a fresh Review Quiz
●	If Engineer has an unfinished Review Quiz from previous week, mark it expired and replace
●	Do not generate Review Quiz for inactive users (is_active=false or no login in 60 days)

7.7 Certificate issuance — AUTOMATIC, no admin action required
This is a first-class feature. Auto-issuance is what makes Academy pitchable to clients. Do not build a manual approval step in v1.

●	Trigger: The instant an Engineer's Topic Quiz submission causes the LAST remaining Module in a Track (for a given Tier) to become COMPLETED
●	The issuance runs in the same request cycle as the quiz submission — no queued job, no delay, no admin approval
●	Certificate ID format: TNX-{YYYY}-{ENGINEER_INITIALS}-{SEQ} where SEQ is a per-engineer sequence number (e.g. TNX-2026-ALS-04 for Ali Sultan's 4th certificate)
●	PDF is rendered server-side (Browsershot or Puppeteer) from an HTML template, A4 landscape
●	PDF is stored in S3-compatible storage; URL is signed with 30-day expiry for engineer downloads, but the verification URL is public and permanent
●	Certificate template renders: engineer full name, track name, tier, date issued, certificate ID, gold seal, two signatures (Director + Lead Instructor names from track config)
●	On issuance: send email to engineer with PDF attached, send in-app notification, appear in 'My Certificates' immediately, appear in Team Lead dashboard
●	Public verification: GET /verify/{certificate_id} (no auth required) returns a page showing certificate details + 'Verified' or 'Revoked' state
●	Revocation: Super Admin only; revoked certs remain in DB, verification page shows 'Revoked' with reason; all revocations logged to audit_log
●	Engineers cannot re-download a revoked certificate PDF

7.8 Edge cases to handle
●	Engineer with 0 Modules assigned — dashboard shows 'Browse available modules' CTA, no error
●	Module with 0 Questions — CANNOT be published; API returns 422 with clear message
●	Question bank smaller than quiz_question_count — use all available, do not error
●	Engineer network drops during quiz — show clear error, allow reconnect; do not attempt local caching in v1
●	Video upload larger than 500MB — chunked upload; show progress; resume support
●	Engineer's team is deleted — reassign to a 'Unassigned' team, do not delete Engineer
●	Two Engineers submit an Attempt at the same instant — no locking issue because each Attempt is scoped to one Engineer

8. Naming Conventions
8.1 Backend
●	Classes: PascalCase — Module, QuestionController, ReviewQuizGenerator
●	Methods: camelCase — generateReviewQuiz(), assignModule()
●	DB tables: snake_case, plural — modules, attempt_responses
●	DB columns: snake_case — concept_tag, correct_option, response_time_ms
●	Routes: kebab-case — /api/v1/review-quiz, /api/v1/admin/audit-log
●	Migrations: timestamp_snake_case_description.php

8.2 Frontend
●	Components: PascalCase — ModuleCard.vue, QuizQuestion.vue
●	Composables: use prefix, camelCase — useQuizState.js, useAuth.js
●	Store modules (Pinia): camelCase — modulesStore, quizStore
●	CSS: TailwindCSS utility classes; custom classes as kebab-case in component-scoped style blocks

8.3 Example data — always use these names in seeds, tests, examples
# Standard example user
{
  "id": 42,
  "email": "ali.sultan@technonex.de",
  "full_name": "Ali Sultan",
  "role": "engineer",
  "team_id": 3
}
 
# DO NOT use these names in generated content:
