9. File Formats
9.1 Video files
●	Accepted formats: MP4 (H.264 + AAC), MOV, WebM
●	Uploaded to Cloudflare Stream via API; Cloudflare handles transcoding and adaptive bitrate
●	Max upload size: 500MB per file
●	Recommended source: 1080p, 30fps, target duration 10–25 minutes per Module

9.2 Attachment files
●	PDF (up to 20MB), PNG/JPG (up to 5MB each), DOCX (up to 10MB)
●	Stored in S3-compatible object storage; served via signed URLs

9.3 MCQ CSV import format
Header row required. UTF-8 encoded. Commas in text must be quoted with double quotes.
question_text,option_a,option_b,option_c,option_d,correct_option,difficulty,concept_tag,explanation
"What is the correct AP mount height?","1.5m","2.5m","3.0m","Ceiling only","B","easy","ap_mount_height","Standard for enterprise WiFi coverage"
"Which command downgrades IOS-XE?","install remove","install rollback","install add file","install downgrade","C","hard","ios_xe_recovery","Full command: install add file flash: activate commit"

Validation rules for CSV import:
●	correct_option must be one of A, B, C, D
●	difficulty must be one of easy, medium, hard
●	concept_tag must be lowercase, alphanumeric with underscores only
●	All text fields required except explanation
●	On any row failure, return per-row errors — do NOT abort the whole import

10. Security, Compliance & Non-Functional
10.1 Authentication
●	Passwords: bcrypt with cost factor 12
●	Sessions: Laravel Sanctum tokens, 30-day expiry, revoke on logout
●	Hosting: one.com VPS (existing Technonex infrastructure)
●	Rate limiting: 60 requests/minute per IP on auth endpoints
●	Login lockout: 5 failed attempts → 15 min lockout

10.2 Authorization
●	Every API endpoint MUST check role and scope (team_id where applicable)
●	do not scatter authorization logic in controllers
●	Team leads and engineers can never access another team's data — enforce at query level, not just view level

10.3 Data protection (GDPR)
●	Hosting: one.com VPS and services (existing Technonex infrastructure — no change required)
●	GDPR compliance is required for the application itself: consent tracking, data export, right to erasure
●	PII in exports must be limited to what the export is for
●	Right to erasure: users.deleted_at soft delete; attempts and audit_log retained per legitimate interest but PII scrubbed after 30 days
●	Data export: Engineer can download their own attempts and progress as JSON

10.4 Video content protection
●	Videos MUST be private (Cloudflare Stream signed URL access only)
●	Signed URL expiry: 4 hours
●	Domain restriction: signed URLs only playable from academy.technonex.de origin
●	Download disabled at HTML5 video element level; recognize that determined users can still screen-record

10.5 Performance targets
●	API response time p95: < 500ms for read endpoints, < 1500ms for write endpoints
●	Video start playback: < 3 seconds on 4G
●	Dashboard load: < 2 seconds
●	Support 500 concurrent Engineers in v1, 5000 in v2 architecture

10.6 Observability
●	Structured logging (JSON) via Node Log with correlation IDs
●	Error tracking: Sentry or similar
●	Uptime monitoring: Better Stack or similar
●	Audit log for every admin action, immutable append-only

11. Anti-Patterns — DO NOT DO THESE
These are things the AI agent MUST NOT do when generating code, schemas, or copy for this project.

●	DO NOT integrate with NexOps in v1. Academy is standalone.
●	DO NOT use YouTube, Vimeo public, or any public video service. Videos are private.
●	DO NOT hardcode UI strings — everything user-facing goes through a translation layer with English and German locales only.
●	DO NOT build a native iOS or Android app in v1. PWA only.
●	DO NOT use 'Hamza' or 'Abdul' as example names anywhere. Use 'Ali Sultan'.
●	DO NOT skip the audit log on admin actions.
●	DO NOT delete Questions hard — always soft delete to preserve historical Attempts.
●	DO NOT mutate an Attempt after it is submitted.
●	DO NOT allow a Module to be published without a video and at least 5 active Questions.
●	DO NOT expose correct_option in Questions payload during a live Quiz.
●	DO NOT let team leads see engineers outside their team_id.
●	DO NOT skip prerequisite checks — but DO respect Admin assignment override.
●	DO NOT build gamification (badges, leaderboards, streaks) in v1.
●	DO NOT add social features (comments, discussions) in v1.
●	DO NOT pick your own color palette — the brand pack (colors, fonts, logos) will be provided separately by Hamza. Do not start UI implementation before that pack is delivered.
●	DO NOT add languages beyond English and German in v1.
●	DO NOT build an offline mode. Assume network is available; graceful error messages are enough.
●	DO NOT make up business rules. If a rule is missing from this document, ASK the human product owner.

12. v1 Acceptance Criteria
v1 is considered DONE when all of the following are true. This is the definition of done, not a nice-to-have list.

12.1 Content management
●	An Admin can create a Module with title, track, tier, description in < 2 minutes
●	An Admin can upload a video to a Module and see it playable in < 15 minutes (including Cloudflare transcode)
●	An Admin can add MCQ Questions individually via form
●	An Admin can bulk-import >= 25 MCQ Questions via CSV in a single upload
●	An Admin can publish a Module only if it has video + >= 5 Questions

12.2 Engineer experience
●	An Engineer can log in on mobile, install as PWA, and access assigned Modules
●	An Engineer can watch a video with resume-from-position and playback speed control
●	An Engineer can take a Topic Quiz after video completion and see immediate per-question feedback
●	An Engineer can retake a failed Topic Quiz after cooldown
●	An Engineer with >= 3 completed Modules receives a Review Quiz weekly
●	An Engineer can view their progress: modules complete, weak concepts, earned certificates

12.3 Team lead experience
●	A Team Lead can view their team's engineers and per-engineer completion status
●	A Team Lead can assign a Module to one or many engineers with a deadline
●	A Team Lead can see per-concept weakness for their team

12.4 System
●	Videos are served via signed URLs that expire in 4 hours
●	All PII data is stored in EU
●	Audit log records every admin write operation
●	Weekly Review Quiz generation runs automatically at Monday 06:00 UTC
●	Overdue check runs nightly and updates assignment status
●	On completing the last Module of a Track, the Engineer receives an auto-issued certificate PDF within seconds, via email + in-app + certificate list
●	Certificate verification URL /verify/{id} is publicly accessible without login
●	Super Admin can revoke a certificate and the verification page reflects the change immediately
13. Open Questions for the Product Owner
These are decisions NOT YET MADE. If your work depends on one of these, ask before assuming.

●	Certificate template design — using placeholder in v1, needs design pass
●	Exact list of Tracks and initial 5 Modules for launch content
●	Notification email templates and sender identity (academy@technonex.de vs noreply@)
●	Whether to support SMS notifications for deadlines (currently: no, email + in-app only)
●	Data retention policy for abandoned attempts (currently: retained indefinitely for analytics)
●	Whether Engineers can browse Modules NOT assigned to them (currently: yes, but cannot start without assignment or self-enroll)
●	Self-enrollment allowed? (currently: no — assignment required)
●	Exact CSV column ordering for Question import (draft in Section 9.3 — confirm with Admin team)
